  "context": {
    "explanation_en": "When building an argument, comparatives support a claim persuasively: 'increasingly important', 'far outweighs', 'is preferable to'. These sound more analytical than simple 'better' or 'more': 'The benefits far outweigh the risks.'",
    "explanation_ko": "논증을 펼칠 때 비교급은 주장을 설득력 있게 뒷받침합니다: 'increasingly important', 'far outweighs', 'is preferable to'. 단순한 'better'나 'more'보다 더 분석적으로 들립니다: 'The benefits far outweigh the risks.'",
    "key_expressions": [
      {
        "en": "The benefits far outweigh the costs.",
        "ko": "이익이 비용을 훨씬 능가해요."
      },
      {
        "en": "Remote work is preferable to commuting for many people.",
        "ko": "많은 사람들에게 재택근무가 통근보다 낫다고 여겨져요."
      },
      {
        "en": "This issue is becoming increasingly important.",
        "ko": "이 문제는 점점 더 중요해지고 있어요."
      }
    ]
  },
